import type { MagicItemDefinition } from "@/engine/types";

// Relics (Alderac Entertainment Group, ©2003, d20 System
// — a 3.0-era book: the cover requires the Dungeons &
// Dragons Player's Handbook, Third Edition), transcribed
// from Shaun's own scanned copy (read visually; the scan
// is image-only), 2026-11-04. The whole book is a single
// chapter of artifact entries, printed pp. 6-124, plus an
// Index (p. 125) that classifies each item by type. The
// book prints NO market price and NO creation
// prerequisites for any relic — these are artifacts, and
// each entry's stat line gives only a Caster Level and
// Weight — so, following the catalog's DMG artifacts
// precedent, every record here is category "artifact"
// with cost "—", its summary opens with the book's own
// Index type word ("Artifact (ring):" etc.), and the
// summary closes with the printed Caster Level / Weight
// line where the entry prints one. A substantial minority
// of entries print no stat line at all; those summaries
// say so instead of inventing values, and the range notes
// (notes-a/b/c/d.md) list them. 3.0 mechanics were
// converted to 3.5 standard in the 2026-11-10 conversion
// pass under Shaun's standing order (e.g. DR 15/+3 →
// DR 15/magic). Faith-, deity-, and
// alignment-tied restrictions are kept as printed.
//
// The 111 Index entries yield 122 records: combined
// entries are split per distinct item/stat block (the
// Chain of Truth, Rod of Honor, and Stone of Justice are
// three records; the Rings of the Three Sisters are four
// — the Maiden, Mother, and Crone rings plus a set record
// for their Combined Powers; the Tomes of Althing are
// four; the Triddic Staff and the Birthstone are two),
// and two records come from inside other entries where
// the book prints a complete extra item: the Shroud of
// Mellayah (in the Cloak of Life's Legend, p. 28) and the
// Boneless weapon special ability (priced at +4 bonus,
// printed in the Pureblood Dagger's Legend, p. 82 — the
// one priced, craftable entry in the book, so it keeps
// its printed price instead of the artifact "—"). Each
// entry's Legend also carries an NPC stat block; those
// are not builder content and were not built (names are
// logged in the range notes). The book additionally
// prints eight feats and two templates inside entries
// and Legends — those live in this pack's feats.ts and
// templates.ts. Book quirks are flagged in the notes and
// the pack report (relics-draft.md): among them, the
// pp. 21-23 stone is "Stone of Justice" in the entry
// title, TOC, and Index but "Stone of Mercy" in its
// mechanics heading and body text (the record is named
// per the title/Index and the summary discloses it), the
// p. 106 heading prints "TEXLES'SCARA" against the
// TOC/Index's "Texes'scara" (heading followed, verified
// at 250 DPI), and the p. 75 heading is singular
// "Nr'duk's Fang" against the Index's plural.
// Summaries are mechanical paraphrases in our own words
// carrying every printed number; no book prose is
// reproduced.

